A||||8||2birds||Fiero's and tranquility||||1||
Z||000000||2birds||11-18-2001||11:59 PM||||After driving my 94 Mustang GT for the last two weeks, I finally drove the Fiero for a few days.  The weather turned nicer again, finally (70's and no rain).  It was so nice to hear the growl of the 2.8, and to have the fun of a 5-speed for once.  The Mustang may be more powerful, but the Fiero is so much more fun to drive.<BR>After cleaning my garage out somewhat, I decided to take in the night sky.  Where else to do it from but the hood of the Fiero.  My sons (ages 4 and 7) joined me, and we must have spent about an hour sprawled on the hood watching the stars and airplanes moving across the night sky.  Amazing how comfortable the front hood can be.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"><P>My world was great for a while.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroMontreal||11-19-2001||12:10 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I gotta try the front hood one of these days!<P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif">   <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||11-19-2001||12:20 AM||||Hood thing sounds fun good. If you have a hardtop, don't sit on the roof! You might end up going through it, the headliner and you'd be back where you started, in the car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. Im just joking! Roof would probably support a person. But im not going to try...<P>Sounds like you had a fun time. I have been going out every night recently and just driving around the country in my fiero. It's one of the things I look forward to at the end of the day.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Brandon86SE||11-19-2001||12:47 AM||||Lying on the hood is great!  I've been known to not be able to fall asleep at night, and take off at 2am just for a relaxing drive, make it to the outskirts of town, or a park or something, lie on the hood and watch the stars, or city lights.  Incredibly relaxing, and helps to get my mind off of stuff!<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||2birds||11-19-2001||09:56 PM||||It's not so peaceful around here to drive in the country at night.  Too many critters from the swamps.<P>When I lived in SE Minnesota as a Navy recruiter, I used to love taking the back roads any time I could.  No traffic, and straight stretches of highway.  You could see for miles in any direction.  I'd take the sunroof out and it was just the big sky above.  Nighttime is the greatest out there.  <BR>The only other time I've seen so many stars is when my sub was running on the surface at night, far away from land.  Virtually no lights at all to interfere with the night sky.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DR650SE||11-19-2001||11:34 PM||||Ever try the movie slide across the hood?  I have once after a good wax and and polish, did so in sweats as to not scratch.  It was pretty slick.  The second time i didit the lil bro was inside the car and thought it would be funny to turn on the lights  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> .  *ouch* no damage but it was kinda funny, i gotta admit.<P>------------------<BR>AIM:  DR650SE<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||1
